  "surprise": "P50-family future-token-set auxiliary (a pretraining-only Linear(384,107) bag head on ln_f(h_t), BCE summed over the 107 token types of the rest of the proof, weight 0.1, next to next-token CE and t+2 MTP; handed-off model unchanged, 9,557,760 params) scored 606/602/577 on seeds 0/1/2: mean 595.0 vs 191-claude's 683.67 (694/694/663), -88.7, paired -88/-92/-86, far below the keep line; the registered falsifier (mean below 660) fired. One of the largest Lean-era losses for a pretraining-only change, and consistent across seeds (~3.5 SE of a 3-seed mean). Pretraining went as registered: 5,233/5,111/5,210 steps (191: 5,362/5,298/5,220; registered 4,950-5,350), 4.5-4.6 epochs, bag_loss 16-21 at 45 s falling to 0.84/0.72/0.90 at 300 s (registered 15-60 -> 0.5-4), final next-token val loss 0.0863/0.0797/0.0875 (191: 0.092/0.082/0.086; no crowding-out of next-token fit, so counter-hypothesis (a) as registered did not show in val loss). Surprise: equal-or-better teacher-forced val loss, but a worse prover and a much worse RL start. Held-out greedy after pretraining 0.9545/0.950/0.954 (191: 0.9705/0.972/0.9585), and expert iteration gained less every round: RL targets solved r2 819/813/848 (191: 1023/926/943), r4 1080/1077/1077 (191: 1189/1160/1142; registered 1,130-1,210, missed). Round 1 was 269/444/505 (191: 682/454/225; not a falsifier). The loss is spread across the eval bins rather than only at the long end (seed 0 >=7/8/9/10/11: 606/516/413/88/14 vs 191 seed 0's 694/594/475/111/27; >=10 88/83/78), L* 11 on all seeds, post-RL greedy 0.988-0.9885. Reading, not established: making the set of remaining proof tokens linearly decodable from the same ln_f state the next-token head reads costs autoregressive proving quality that val CE does not measure, and RL cannot recover it in 4 rounds; the bag's size is also a remaining-length cue fitted to <= 6-line proofs (counter-hypothesis b), which may explain why RL gains less, but 3 seeds cannot separate these. Contrast with t+2 MTP (+12 in 136, -27 when removed in 193), which predicts through its own block rather than a linear readout of the trunk's final state. Not worth a lower-weight follow-up without a mechanism check. Totals 1692/1884/1863 s of 2400; seeds 1/2 ran on slower pods (172-182 samples/s in round 2). Bench before registering (60 s, one A40): 19.8 steps/s after setup vs 191's 20.8.",
